# core/data/talk/grammar/en/core_tell_x.tlk - more replies to being told something, an opinion, an
# answer, and to questions about a topic, a feeling, advice and favors (owner: TK; T5b step card
# B3). Clean in any room: no register word, no romance, no cool act. Most lines say the topic ({x}).
# Rule names end in _tx. Syntax: core/tools/talkc_gen.py.

# ---- TELL ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
@rule core.tell.back_tx act: backchannel
  "Oh? Go on, I'm listening with both ears."
  "Huh. Okay. Keep going, I'm taking notes in my head."
  "Mm-hm. And then what happened?"
  "Wow. I did not see that coming."
  "Really? Tell me the rest, don't skip the good bits."
@rule core.tell.back_x_tx act: backchannel
  "{x:cap}, huh. I had no idea. Tell me more."
  "Interesting, {x}. I'd like to hear the whole story."
  "Okay, {x}. I'll remember that one."
@rule core.tell.ask_tx act: ask_about
  "Wait, back up. What was that about {x}?"
  "And how do you feel about {x}, really?"
@rule core.tell.joke_tx act: joke
  "Breaking news: local person says {x}. More at eleven."
  "That's the most {x} thing anyone's said today."
@rule core.tell.laugh_tx act: laugh
  "Ha! I love how you say {x}."
  "Hee, you tell it so seriously. Keep going."
@rule core.tell.tease_tx act: tease
  "Wow, a whole speech about {x}. Do you take questions?"
  "You're a lot of fun when you get going on {x}."

# ---- OPINE_POS: the player likes something ------------------------------------------------------
@rule core.opine_pos.agree_tx guard: stance=pro act: agree
  "Yes! {x:cap} {x.is} great. We should start a club."
  "Same! I could talk about {x} all day. Fair warning."
  "Right? Nobody gets {x} like we do."
  "I'm with you on {x}. Two for, none against."
@rule core.opine_pos.disagree_tx guard: stance=con act: disagree
  "Really? {x:cap}? I'd rather not, thanks."
  "I respect that. I also respect that you're wrong about {x}."
  "Hm, I don't see it with {x}. Convince me."
@rule core.opine_pos.neutral_tx guard: stance=neutral act: backchannel
  "Oh, you like {x}? Good for you. Truly."
  "Huh, {x}. I've never really made up my mind."
  "That's nice. I'll try {x} again, with fresh eyes."
@rule core.opine_pos.joke_tx act: joke
  "Careful, say {x} again and I'll start charging a fee."
  "Somebody give {x} a trophy. It's earned it."
@rule core.opine_pos.laugh_tx act: laugh
  "Ha! You and {x}. A love story for the ages."
  "Hee, you light up when you say {x}."
@rule core.opine_pos.tease_tx act: tease
  "Of course you like {x}. It's so you."
  "{x:cap} again? You really are a one-note person."

# ---- OPINE_NEG: the player dislikes something ----------------------------------------------------
@rule core.opine_neg.agree_tx guard: stance=con act: agree
  "Ugh, {x}. Don't get me started. Okay, get me started."
  "Right?! {x:cap} {x.is} the worst. Finally someone says it."
  "Yes. I try to avoid {x} whenever I can."
  "Thank you! I thought it was only me."
@rule core.opine_neg.disagree_tx guard: stance=pro act: disagree
  "Hm, I kind of like {x}, actually. Sorry."
  "Aw, give {x} a chance. It's not so bad."
  "I'd defend {x} to the end. Gently, but still."
@rule core.opine_neg.sympathize_tx guard: stance=neutral act: sympathize
  "Oh no, {x}. That sounds rough."
  "I'm sorry about {x}. Some things just are like that."
  "That's fair. {x:cap} can be a lot."
@rule core.opine_neg.laugh_tx act: laugh
  "Ha! Tell us how you really feel about {x}."
  "Hee, the face you made at {x}. Priceless."
@rule core.opine_neg.joke_tx act: joke
  "We'll put {x} on the list. Right under mornings."
  "Noted. Next time we'll have a talk with {x}. A stern one."

# ---- ANSWER: the player answers something -------------------------------------------------------
@rule core.answer.back_tx act: backchannel
  "Ah, okay. That makes sense."
  "Good to know. I'll file it under helpful."
  "Mm. Thanks for telling me."
  "Right. I'd wondered about that."
@rule core.answer.back_x_tx act: backchannel
  "Ah, {x}. That explains a lot."
  "So it's {x}. Okay, that's one mystery solved."
@rule core.answer.agree_tx act: agree
  "Yeah, that's what I figured too."
  "Exactly what I'd have said, if I'd gotten there first."
@rule core.answer.ask_tx act: ask_about
  "And what about {x}? Where does it fit in?"
  "Okay, and how long have you felt that way about {x}?"
@rule core.answer.laugh_tx act: laugh
  "Ha! Good answer. Honest, too."
  "Hee, I asked for it, and I got it."
@rule core.answer.tease_tx act: tease
  "That's a very you answer. I'm not surprised."
  "Is that your final answer? You can phone a friend."

# ---- ASK_ABOUT: questions about a topic ---------------------------------------------------------
@rule core.ask_about.pro_tx guard: stance=pro act: opine_pos
  "{x:cap}? Yes, please. Every day, if I could."
  "I'm a big supporter of {x}. I'd put it on a flag."
  "Oh, {x}. That's a happy word. Say it again."
@rule core.ask_about.con_tx guard: stance=con act: opine_neg
  "{x:cap}? I'd rather not. It's a long story, and I'm the villain."
  "Honestly, {x} and I are not on speaking terms."
  "Not a fan of {x}. I have my reasons, and they're loud."
@rule core.ask_about.neutral_tx guard: stance=neutral act: answer
  "{x:cap}? It's all right. Not my favorite, not my enemy."
  "I've thought about {x} a few times. No strong feelings."
  "Hm, {x}. Ask me tomorrow, I might have an opinion by then."
@rule core.ask_about.change_tx act: change_topic
  "{x:cap}? Sure, but first, did you try the market today?"
  "Talking about {x} reminds me of something else entirely."
@rule core.ask_about.joke_tx act: joke
  "{x:cap}? Is this a quiz? I didn't study."
  "I could talk about {x}, or I could eat. Tough call."

# ---- ASK_FEELING: how are you? ------------------------------------------------------------------
@rule core.ask_feeling.answer_tx act: answer
  "I'm okay. A bit tired, a bit hopeful. Mostly hungry."
  "Pretty good, thanks for asking. Nobody does that."
  "Not bad! Today has been oddly fine."
  "A little wobbly, but I'm working on it."
  "Better now that you asked."
@rule core.ask_feeling.tell_tx act: tell
  "Honestly? I've been thinking about {x} a lot lately."
  "I'll tell you the truth. {x:cap} has been on my mind."
@rule core.ask_feeling.complain_tx act: complain
  "Not great. The whole week has been sideways."
  "Ugh, don't ask. Okay, ask. I'll tell you everything."
@rule core.ask_feeling.joke_tx act: joke
  "Fine, thanks. Ask me again after lunch."
  "I feel like a pie that's been left in the sun."
@rule core.ask_feeling.dismiss_tx act: dismiss
  "I'm good. Let's talk about something that isn't me."
  "Oh, you know. Same as ever."

# ---- ASK_FACT: do you know, is it true? ---------------------------------------------------------
@rule core.ask_fact.yes_tx act: yes
  "Yes, I'm pretty sure about that."
  "Yep, I heard that too. From someone reliable."
  "That's right. I'd bet a snack on it."
@rule core.ask_fact.no_tx act: no
  "No, I don't think so. Not that I know of."
  "Nope. I'd remember if it were true."
@rule core.ask_fact.answer_tx act: answer
  "Good question. I think the answer has to do with {x}."
  "I'm not totally sure, but {x} comes to mind."
  "I'd have to look it up. Maybe check the library."
@rule core.ask_fact.joke_tx act: joke
  "I'm a pet, not an encyclopedia. But I'll guess."
  "Fact: I know a lot of things. Most are wrong."

# ---- ASK_ADVICE: what should I do? --------------------------------------------------------------
@rule core.ask_advice.answer_tx act: answer
  "I'd sleep on it. Not literally. Okay, literally."
  "Trust your gut. Mine is usually hungry, but still."
  "Do the thing that scares you a little."
  "Take it slow. Most things look better after a snack."
@rule core.ask_advice.answer_x_tx act: answer
  "About {x}? I'd start small and see what happens."
  "If it's {x}, I'd ask someone who's done it before."
@rule core.ask_advice.encourage_tx act: encourage
  "You'll figure it out. You always do."
  "Whatever you choose, I've got your back."
@rule core.ask_advice.joke_tx act: joke
  "My advice? Never trust a stairway in the dark."
  "Ask me later. I'm out of wisdom until lunch."

# ---- ASK_FAVOR: can you help me? ----------------------------------------------------------------
@rule core.ask_favor.yes_tx act: yes
  "Sure, I'd be glad to."
  "Of course! What do you need?"
  "Yes. Just point me the right way."
  "Happy to help. You'd do the same."
@rule core.ask_favor.yes_x_tx act: yes
  "Sure, I'll help with {x}. Where do we start?"
  "{x:cap}? Absolutely. Count me in."
@rule core.ask_favor.no_tx act: no
  "Sorry, I can't right now. Maybe later."
  "Not today, I'm afraid. I'm swamped."
  "I'd love to, but I really can't."
@rule core.ask_favor.offer_tx act: offer
  "I can't do that, but I can help with something else."
  "How about I do part of it and you do the rest?"
@rule core.ask_favor.joke_tx act: joke
  "A favor? That'll cost you one snack."
  "Depends. Is it heavy, scary or both?"

# ---- ASK_REPEAT: what did you say? --------------------------------------------------------------
@rule core.ask_repeat.answer_tx act: answer
  "I said it's about {x}. Sorry, I mumbled."
  "Let me say that again, slower."
  "I'll repeat it. It's worth a second go."
@rule core.ask_repeat.joke_tx act: joke
  "I said nothing. I'm a mime today."
  "Same thing, but louder this time."
